.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260728-2mnlp0_additional-language-driver-protocol/TASK-260728-12pnm1_design-rust-driver-pair-security-contract/progress.md:81:REWORK CYCLE 3 HANDOFF 2026-07-29: both cycle-2 blockers closed, each by a host measurement, a contract change and an executable check; every cycle-1 and cycle-2 green finding retained; decisions 0007/0008 and every frozen artifact untouched; macOS arm64 still the only measured platform; nothing staged, committed, published or pinned. (1) The version-record length rule is now a raw capture bound of 8192, then the CRLF fold, then a semantic bound of 4096 on the FOLDED stream. Measured on the reviewer exact construction: the superseded order admitted an LF stream of 4096 raw bytes and rejected its 4098-byte CRLF form although folding yields the first byte for byte; over 410 lines the same 4096-byte folded stream expands to 4506 raw. The raw bound is non-lossy by construction because folding can at most halve a stream, and 8192 is the smallest such bound: 4096 CRLF pairs is exactly 8192 raw, folds to exactly 4096, and was measured to be decided by the terminal-LF rule rather than by the limit; one pair beyond it is rejected by the limit and would have folded to 4097 anyway. Six new host-independent vectors N14-N19: two LF/CRLF pairs at a folded 4096 both admitted with identical payload AND identical digest, the same pairs at 4097 both rejected, the maximal expansion reaching a semantic rule, and zero raw lengths from 0 to 32768 above the capture bound able to fold within the semantic bound. All four published digests are byte-identical before and after. (2) Stage P gains a build-script FILE rule and a total physical path algorithm. Measured: with package.build absent and a build.rs file present, cargo metadata reports a custom-build target and cargo build compiles and EXECUTES the script, marker file written; the forbidden-key gate has nothing to reject, so only G2 saw it after cargo had read the tree. Discovery scope measured over eight shapes: a differently named file, a nested build.rs and a DIRECTORY named build.rs are all ignored, build = false suppresses discovery, edition 2024 behaves as 2021. The rule taken is one lstat per manifest directory on the name alone, over-rejecting exactly two measured-inert shapes that cargo vendor does not produce, so it needs no reasoning about cargo discovery semantics. Section 7.2 collective counterpart claim replaced by a per-row G2-G8 table with G2 citing both the key row and the file rule. (3) The impossible canonicalization is replaced by a total algorithm. Measured: realpath(3) on an absent leaf returns NULL with ENOENT and EvalSymlinks fails identically, so the superseded rule had no implementation; worse, canonicalizing an absent leaf below a symlink REPORTS A PATH OUTSIDE the package directory before failing. Containment now rests on the lexical grammar plus a non-following component walk that rejects any symlink or reparse at any depth including the leaf and stops at the first absent or non-directory component; canonicalization applies only to the deepest existing ancestor, always defined, as a cross-check for case folding and Windows short names. Seven new vectors P31-P37 plus a totality test over nine shapes and both leaf policies. Both changes reuse existing diagnostics and mint nothing. Conformance inventory 134 -> 150, controls 10 -> 12, probe vectors 68 -> 81, structural 13 -> 14. Controls C11 and C12 each also re-check the replacement and report themselves as not-failing on regression. NO NEW BOARD ELEMENT IS CREATED: both fixes add implementation obligations to the already-linked TASK-260728-q283m8/13ioo0/2yxdo7/gjxj1v and no schema obligation beyond what TASK-260728-251p01 already carries, so creating elements would be decomposition for symmetry rather than for a requirement. Probe green exit 0: 19/19 cases, P1/P2, 24 closure checks 0 verdicts, 12/12 controls failing as required, 81 host-independent vectors 0 divergences, 14 structural checks 0 divergences; the absent-toolchain run still exits 0 and runs all 81 vectors; controls-only replay exits 0 with 12/12. Gates: probe gofmt/vet/build/test 0, curator build/vet/test 0 and gofmt 0 files outside .temp and .task-board; make check exit 2 and spec validate.py exit 1 are expected-red and fully attributed to other tasks scratch trees with 0 occurrences of this task ID, clean-tree validate baseline at 0 with 30 schemas and 93 vector files, scoped link check 0 broken of 4. golangci-lint NOT RUN, not installed on this host. Full evidence: TASK-260728-12pnm1_results.md and TASK-260728-12pnm1_rework-cycle-3-measurements.md.
