.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260728-2mnlp0_additional-language-driver-protocol/TASK-260728-12pnm1_design-rust-driver-pair-security-contract/progress.md:97:REWORK CYCLE 4 HANDOFF 2026-07-29: both cycle-3 blockers closed, each by a host measurement, a contract change and an executable check; every cycle-1, cycle-2 and cycle-3 green finding retained; decisions 0007/0008 and every frozen artifact untouched; macOS arm64 still the only measured platform; nothing staged, committed, published or pinned. (1) The profile process. Reproduced exactly: [profile.release] debug=2 plus split-debuginfo="packed" resolves a PATH-selected dsymutil under the exact pinned pipeline and cargo still exits 0. The full stable key set was swept over 62 build roots and exactly one key reaches an executable outside the closure. Two further measurements make the obvious fix wrong: an UNRECOGNIZED value ("wat", "", "PACKED") makes cargo forward NO -Csplit-debuginfo at all - captured from a logging RUSTC wrapper - and rustc own aarch64-apple-darwin default is packed, so dsymutil runs anyway with no warning and exit 0, which bypasses any deny-list naming packed; and an unknown profile key is accepted by cargo silently, which defeats any key deny-list. cargo metadata reports no profile information, so no row G0-G11 can ever see this surface. The fix is two-layered: new reference section 4.7 is a closed POSITIVE allowlist - three table shapes, eleven keys each with its own value set, split-debuginfo rejected outright at every value - decided over every manifest in the build root before any cargo process; and section 6 pins -Csplit-debuginfo=<pin> in CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS, a manager constant per operating system, off on macOS, measured to give 0 PATH resolutions for packed, an unrecognized value, the empty string and a package override, each of which resolves dsymutil without it. The pin answers a TOOLCHAIN default no package byte selects, so it is load-bearing rather than hygiene. Over-rejection bounded by corpus: of 506 published crate manifests in the host registry cache 37 carry a profile table, they use seven keys between them, ZERO use split-debuginfo, and all 37 pass. A profile table in a path or vendored dependency was measured inert and is rejected anyway as a stated over-rejection. Also measured: the vendor checksum is not a pre-compile gate - editing a vendored Cargo.toml without repairing .cargo-checksum.json leaves cargo metadata at exit 0 and fails only at cargo build. Diagnostic reused: build_rust_manifest_key_forbidden. Section 2.1 now states that three executables is a conclusion of the gates rather than a property of Rust; acceptance test section 13.1 gains step 4, the profile replay, whose unpinned run is its own control and is required to fire. (2) The G11 admitted set. The superseded text required every reported manifest_path and src_path to be in a set it never constructed, so an ordinary auto-discovered src/main.rs had no verdict and an implementation had to either reject positive builds or copy Cargo target auto-discovery into the security boundary. New section 4.8 defines A as every path the link-free section 4.1 walk enumerated under R plus every leaf section 4.3 admitted and permitted to be absent. Sufficiency is MEASURED over fourteen discovery shapes: every path cargo reports is either an existing file under R or a path a key declared, and a name-only target with no discoverable file makes the graph exit 101 rather than report a phantom src_path, so there is no third case. Unreachable manifests, missing default leaves and the root single-bin rule are each answered explicitly; G9 keeps target shape, A keeps containment. Policy object gains two const members, profile_policy=closed-grammar-v1 and debuginfo_packaging=pinned-off; the pin changes produced bytes because CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS participates in cargo fingerprint, measured byte-identical under one pin and different across pins, so it enters cache identity. Windows and Linux pin values are new qualification obligations and are explicitly NOT assumed to be off, because MSVC writes a PDB through the pinned linker and Linux packed runs an external dwp. Conformance inventory 150 -> 195 vectors, controls 12 -> 15, probe host-independent vectors 81 -> 124, structural checks 14 -> 16, new diagnostics NONE. NO NEW BOARD ELEMENT IS CREATED: both fixes add implementation obligations to the already-linked TASK-260728-q283m8/13ioo0/2yxdo7/gjxj1v and two further const members inside the policy object TASK-260728-251p01 was already going to mint, so creating elements would be decomposition for symmetry rather than for a requirement. Probe green exit 0: 19/19 cases, P1/P2, 24 closure checks 0 verdicts, 15/15 controls failing as required (C13 profiles-admitted-wholesale, C14 packed-deny-list, C15 superseded-G11-admitted-set are new), 124 host-independent vectors 0 divergences, 16 structural checks 0 divergences; the absent-toolchain run still exits 0 and runs all 124 vectors; controls-only replay exits 0 with 15/15. Gates: probe gofmt/vet/build/test 0 from the extracted tarball, curator build/vet/test 0 and gofmt 0 files outside .temp and .task-board; make check exit 2 and spec validate.py exit 1 are expected-red and fully attributed to other tasks scratch trees with 0 occurrences of this task ID, clean-tree validate baseline exit 0 with 30 schemas and 93 vector files, scoped link check 0 broken of 4. golangci-lint NOT RUN, not installed on this host. Full evidence: TASK-260728-12pnm1_results.md and TASK-260728-12pnm1_rework-cycle-4-measurements.md.
